This function is meant to return the index of the last element ≤ t in a sorted list. What happens when you call `f([1, 2], 2)`?

```python
def f(a, t):
    lo, hi = 0, len(a) - 1
    while lo < hi:
        mid = (lo + hi) // 2
        if a[mid] <= t:
            lo = mid
        else:
            hi = mid - 1
    return lo
```

Lomuto partitioning uses the last element as pivot and moves elements smaller than it to the front, then swaps the pivot into place. What is the array and returned index after partitioning `[3, 8, 2, 5, 1, 4, 7, 6]`?

```python
def partition(a, lo, hi):
    p = a[hi]; i = lo
    for j in range(lo, hi):
        if a[j] < p:
            a[i], a[j] = a[j], a[i]; i += 1
    a[i], a[hi] = a[hi], a[i]
    return i
```

