This finds a peak element (strictly greater than its neighbours). Which index does it return?

```python
def peak(nums):
    lo, hi = 0, len(nums) - 1
    while lo < hi:
        mid = (lo + hi) // 2
        if nums[mid] > nums[mid + 1]:
            hi = mid
        else:
            lo = mid + 1
    return lo

